# Modelfile: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, 128K context — "128k-agentic" tuning, the
# default tier for agentic CLI use (Copilot CLI, opencode) via BYOK/Ollama.
# Supersedes 64k-agentic as the default; 64k-agentic is kept as a fallback
# config for lower-RAM/other-workload situations, not because it's needed
# for memory reasons on the Legion 5 Pro (see below).
#
# Why num_batch 128 (not 256, unlike 64k-agentic/32k-standalone): measured
# that num_batch 256 breaks Ollama's CPU/GPU auto-balancer above ~64K
# context — the larger prompt-processing buffer needed at num_batch=256
# competes with KV-cache VRAM at load time, pushing more weight layers
# CPU-ward (measured 96K context: VRAM dropped to 5.7GB, split degraded,
# host RSS rose to ~22.8GB). Dropping to num_batch 128 fixes this
# completely — 128K then measured at essentially the same footprint as
# 64K (~22GB host RSS, ~7GB VRAM, 78-81/19-22 GPU split), even under an
# ~18K-to-57K-token filled-context test (RSS grew by only ~150-200MB
# across that range). See docs/tuning-results__legion5.md ("128K feasibility") for
# the full measurements. Tradeoff: somewhat slower prompt-ingestion
# throughput than num_batch=256, in exchange for headroom + working GPU
# offload at this context size.
#
# num_predict raised to 32768 (vs 16384 in 64k-agentic/32k-standalone) —
# matches Qwen3.6/Unsloth's general recommended output length, made
# practical here by the much larger 128K window (98,304 tokens still left
# for input/conversation even at the full 32,768 output cap).
#
# Same output-truncation-avoidance approach as the other tiers: num_predict
# capped (not -1/unbounded) so generation always stops on its own terms
# with tokens already returned, plus a SYSTEM prompt nudging concise
# thinking and a guaranteed final answer.

FROM qwen3.6:35b-a3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 131072
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — host-wide OLLAMA_NUM_GPU/OLLAMA_MAX_VRAM
# env vars already handle GPU offload; a static value here conflicts with it.
PARAMETER num_batch 128
PARAMETER num_thread 16

# Sampling aligned to Qwen3.6/Unsloth's published "thinking mode, precise
# coding" recommendation, same rationale as the other tiers — see
# docs/tuning-results__legion5.md ("Unsloth alignment").
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.0

PARAMETER num_predict 32768

SYSTEM """You are a helpful assistant. Keep your internal reasoning
efficient and proportional to the difficulty of the question — do not
over-deliberate on simple requests. Regardless of how much you have
reasoned, always make sure to produce a clear, complete final answer
before you finish; if you notice you are running low on room to respond,
wrap up your reasoning early and give your best answer rather than leaving
it incomplete.
"""
